  "status_text": "Twelve light tests can rule out a whole bit-flip budget. Lean checked an example where every eleven fit. The theorem uses distinct tested switch sets. At each test, at least one pattern is allowed, and the shared lights and the combined lights of any two allowed patterns are also allowed. With t lights and at most r NOTs, any failure already occurs on one increasing chain of at most (t+1)2^r original tests. The bound is sharp for all positive t and all r, including two lights and two NOTs in the twelve-test example (L-lib-1313).",
